---
import { moduleFragments } from '../../data/meet-builder';
---

<section class="meet-module meet-practice" data-ec-module="02" data-ec-movement="orient" data-ec-intensity="2" aria-labelledby={moduleFragments.practice}>
  <p class="meet-kicker">Practice / responsibility</p>
  <h2 id={moduleFragments.practice}>One person is responsible for the direction and the release.</h2>
  <span class="meet-circuit-rail" data-circuit-label="responsibility" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <div class="meet-practice-grid">
    <article data-ec-node="direction">
      <h3>Candidate research-lab posture: an operating commitment.</h3>
      <p>It means framing focused questions, building or testing small proofs, recording evidence and uncertainty, and returning results for review.</p>
    </article>
    <article data-ec-node="connection">
      <h3>Candidate creative-hub posture: a connective center.</h3>
      <p>It joins selected software, publishing, visual, musical, and narrative work without claiming that every medium is active, available, or mastered.</p>
    </article>
    <article data-ec-node="contribution">
      <h3>Person-led does not erase assistance.</h3>
      <p>Human intention, selection, judgment, verification, and release remain identifiable. Material tools and collaborators are disclosed for each artifact.</p>
    </article>
    <article data-ec-node="scale">
      <h3>The scale stays literal.</h3>
      <p>This candidate posture is not a team, collective, membership community, staffed studio, facility, accredited lab, or source of generalizable results.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
